{
    "background_story": "Ernesto was a charismatic businessman known for his firm and confident handshake. Growing up in a small town, he learned the importance of a good handshake from his father, a respected local merchant. Ernesto's handshake was more than just a greeting - it was a sign of respect, trust, and sealing a deal. He made a point to research the handshake customs of every country he visited, adapting his style to show respect for different cultures. One fateful day, Ernesto's handshake helped him close a major business deal with a Japanese investor, who was impressed by Ernesto's knowledge of the traditional Japanese bow and handshake. The deal propelled Ernesto's company to international success, and his handshake became legendary in business circles.",
